Package: fitgen
----------------
Version 1.0.2:
* Added calculation of Wedderburn, Farrington and Fletcher estimators for overdispersion
* Modified estimation of common Phi in GroupedCommonBlissOwen with a different estimated value for each case

Version 1.0.4:
* Change of names of several function and inclusion of both models under general function FitGLM

Version 1.0.5:
* Preparation to include the R function SelectiveFit as part of the package
* Modification of the return parameters of GroupedCommonBlissOwen from list to list of lists

Version 1.0.6:
* R function SelectiveFit added to the R-source part of the package
* Allowed model names are now Poisson and NB2

Version 1.0.7
* Added access to overdispersion estimation methods implemented in EdgeR

Version 1.0.8
* Added function modelFit in file R/inference.R

Version 1.0.9
* Added logistic regression as a possible model. Change in the names of the models.
* Added a second parameter to the FitGenSetDebug to ask to debugging at a lower level (numerical algorithms)
* Function FitGLM does not exist anymore. It has been divided in two cases: FitGLMInd and FitGLMWithNei
for fitting of a model with or without neighbours.

Version 1.1.1
* Corrected to make the package pass the CRAN tests
* Modified to return NULL when the extended model cannot be fitted not even with one neighbour.

Version 1.1.2
* Added parameters to GroupedCommonBlissOwen to limit (by trimming) the rows considered around each one to estimate Phi.

